-- title:
--   The transported measure on unipotent N(A_ℚ)⊂ GL₃ is Haar
-- statement:
--   Work with the adele ring $\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ carrying its Borel $\sigma$-algebra and the additive Haar measure `adelicAddHaar`, and with $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})$ carrying its Borel $\sigma$-algebra `glBorel`. Let `unipotentSubgroup3` be the subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})$ generated by the image of the map sending a triple $(x,y,z)$ of adeles to the unit $n(x,y,z)$ with matrix $\begin{pmatrix}1&x&z\\0&1&y\\0&0&1\end{pmatrix}$ and explicit inverse $\begin{pmatrix}1&-x&xy-z\\0&1&-y\\0&0&1\end{pmatrix}$, the subgroup being given the induced measurable structure. Let `unipotentHaar3` be the pushforward, along $(x,y,z)\mapsto n(x,y,z)$ viewed as an element of that subgroup, of the product measure $\mathrm{d}x\,\mathrm{d}y\,\mathrm{d}z$ of three copies of the additive Haar measure on $\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}$. The assertion is that `unipotentHaar3` is a Haar measure on the group `unipotentSubgroup3`, i.e. it is left invariant under multiplication, finite on compact sets, and strictly positive on non-empty open sets.
--
--   This records that the natural coordinate measure on the upper triangular unipotent subgroup $N(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})\subset \mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})$ is a left Haar measure, so that integrals over $N$ in the Whittaker-theoretic part of the argument may be computed in the adelic coordinates $(x,y,z)$. It is used in the computations of Whittaker integrals over the torus and the corresponding quotient measure estimates.
